Third-party material
--------------------

Parts of the x86-64 backend follow Firecracker
(https://github.com/firecracker-microvm/firecracker), Copyright Amazon.com,
Inc. or its affiliates, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The
files that do so say where, in their module documentation:

  src/boot_x86.rs    mirrors the arch::x86_64 kernel loader
  src/layout_x86.rs  the same guest memory layout constants
  src/machine_x86.rs the same vCPU and machine bring-up shape
  src/mptable.rs     an MP table of the same small shape (MP spec 1.4)
  src/virtio.rs      the virtio queue and descriptor conventions
  src/sandbox.rs     the confinement goal, by a different mechanism

Confinement on Linux uses seccompiler, the rust-vmm crate extracted from
Firecracker, under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The filter files in
resources/seccomp/ are written in seccompiler's JSON schema. Their content is
ours: resources/seccomp/README.md explains what we deliberately did not carry
over from Firecracker's filters, and why.

The remaining dependencies and their licences are resolved by Cargo and
checked in CI by cargo-deny; see deny.toml and Cargo.toml.
